{"id": "EUVD-2026-93195", "enisaUuid": "55909a7e-d3a0-3a6f-b417-c58969e708c0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\n9p: Fix v9fs_issue_write() to update i_size and remote_i_size\n\nFix v9fs_issue_write() to update i_size and remote_i_size to the new size\nof the server file if we made it larger, using the start fpos and the count\nreturned by p9_client_write() to calculate the new minimum file size.\n\nThis assumes that if the 9P server makes a short write (say it hits\nENOSPC), a reduced count is returned.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aeb1fe55583836744aef11fbfa2a09122aa9816c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88871ab548c1d7b11cde9b04063f3c1c6fbd7039", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cd92e3392bdd14568e9e44aec1ac05e1fcd62e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c60ae98c5aa64021751b38ab1313b19d620bf640"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98267", "GHSA-87v5-rjqw-6p7m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "115d40d9-2c2a-39a7-9f8d-6c61228265b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2cadbd43-b335-3a93-9c0f-36cc2c0ad7c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fb70e7275a61dd404f684370e1add7fe0ebe9c5 <88871ab548c1d7b11cde9b04063f3c1c6fbd7039"}, {"id": "3f25dbe2-952b-32e1-9282-6285ad2be41f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fb70e7275a61dd404f684370e1add7fe0ebe9c5 <aeb1fe55583836744aef11fbfa2a09122aa9816c"}, {"id": "72c261d9-5dd2-30e8-8d0d-8598563bc05f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "8783547b-5417-3165-bdf0-c14cb5fa04ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "8d7b1ed0-9e45-39cb-998a-768acf1257a6", "product": {"